⚙️ Installation & Setup
1. Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/Radhika242005/FemCare.git

Navigate into the project:

cd FemCare
2. Create a Python Virtual Environment

Windows:

python -m venv venv

Activate it:

venv\Scripts\activate

You should see:

(venv)

in the terminal.

3. Install Dependencies

If requirements.txt is available:

pip install -r requirements.txt

If it does not exist yet, install the required Flask packages according to the backend configuration.

4. Configure the Database

Create the required MySQL database.

Example:

CREATE DATABASE femcare;

Configure the database connection in the backend configuration.

Do not commit passwords or secret credentials to GitHub.

Use environment variables where appropriate.

Example:

DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
DB_NAME=femcare
5. Start the Flask Backend

Navigate to the backend:

cd backend

Run the Flask application:

python app.py

The backend should normally be available at:

http://127.0.0.1:5000
6. Open the Frontend

Open the frontend pages using a local web server.

For example, with VS Code Live Server:

Open frontend/pages/login.html

Start the application from the login page.

🔗 Main API Endpoints

The application uses REST APIs between the frontend and Flask backend.

Authentication
POST /api/auth/register
POST /api/auth/login
Period Tracking
POST /api/periods
GET  /api/periods/history/<user_id>
GET  /api/periods/trend/<user_id>
Health Tracking
POST /api/health
GET  /api/health/<user_id>
Food & Nutrition
POST /api/food/analyze
Pregnancy
POST /api/pregnancy/analyze
PCOS
POST /api/pcos/analyze
Dataset Insights
GET /api/datasets/menstrual/analysis

Endpoint names may vary slightly depending on the final backend route configuration.

📊 Data Processing

FemCare uses recorded user information and reference datasets to generate wellness-oriented insights.

The system can analyze information such as:

Menstrual Cycle
       ↓
Health Logs
       ↓
Lifestyle Information
       ↓
Nutrition Information
       ↓
Reference Dataset
       ↓
Analysis
       ↓
Trends & Recommendations

The application does not present these results as medical diagnoses.

🔐 Privacy & Security

FemCare is designed to keep user health information within the application's database and backend system.

Recommended security practices include:

Never commit .env files
Never commit database passwords
Never commit API keys
Use environment variables for secrets
Validate user input on the backend
Use parameterized SQL queries
Restrict access to user-specific records
Keep authentication credentials secure
⚠️ Medical Disclaimer

FemCare is a health monitoring and wellness support application.

The information provided by the application is intended for:

Wellness tracking
Educational purposes
Reference dataset analysis
Lifestyle awareness
Personal health record tracking

FemCare does not replace professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.

Pregnancy, PCOS, menstrual, nutrition, and other health-related results should not be interpreted as a medical diagnosis.

Users should consult a qualified healthcare professional for medical concerns.

🎯 Project Objectives

The main objectives of FemCare are:

To provide a centralized women's health monitoring platform.
To allow users to track menstrual cycles.
To maintain personal health history.
To identify changes in health-related parameters.
To provide nutrition and lifestyle insights.
To provide reference-based PCOS and pregnancy screening information.
To analyze reference health datasets.
To provide personalized wellness recommendations.
To help users understand their health patterns over time.
